# Interaction latency, part 2 of 3: session switch, popup, attachment, sheet. Split from part 1 because these need their own fixture and the
# nine together exceed the runner's per-script budget.
#
# Same rules: arm on ink that is not on screen, do the input, read the wait.
# docs/perf/LATENCY.md has the budgets and the measurements.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2","t9"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_PICK_FILE_TEST='tests/fixtures/attachments/sample.pdf;tests/fixtures/attachments/sample.md'

require_thread t2
wait_frames 20

# 5. SESSION SWITCH -- a second open tab, measured to content only that thread
#    has, so the number is the switch and not the tab strip repainting.
watch_ink session_switch text "Kicked 41"
click_text "kicker-tick"
wait_frames 14
expect_latency session_switch 11

# 6. POPUP -- the model picker over a live thread. A popup draws over the pane
#    it belongs to; the sheet below takes the window, which is why they are
#    measured and budgeted apart.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
watch_ink popup_open ui slash_menu
type "/"
wait_frames 10
expect_latency popup_open 5
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 8

# 8. ATTACHMENT -- the production picker seam: the control runs the picker, the
#    file is retained, and the composer draws a chip through the same decode
#    cache the transcript's inline images use. Measured to the first chip.
#    HANABI_PICK_FILE_TEST only stands in for the native dialog; everything
#    after it is the real retain-and-render path.
focus_ui composer_attach
expect_focused composer_attach
watch_ink attachment ui attach_chip_0
enter
wait_frames 20
expect_latency attachment 9

# 9. SHEET / MODAL -- hanabi's rename modal, reached the way a person reaches
#    it. It takes the window, scrims what is behind it and takes the keyboard.
right_click_text "kicker-tick"
wait_frames 6
watch_ink sheet_open ui rename_panel
click_ui row_menu_rename
wait_frames 12
expect_latency sheet_open 6
